<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8398" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cisseus</span></b> , ĕi,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κισσεύς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A king of Thrace;</i> acc. to a later myth, <i>father of Hecuba</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 5,
				537</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">911</span></i>; who is on this
			account called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cissēïs</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				320</span></i> Serv.; 10, 705.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A companion of Turnus</i>, acc.
			Cissea, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 10, 317</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
